1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,825
This is Opportunity Scout. It decides
whether a job or a research programme

2
00:00:05,825 --> 00:00:11,571
is worth applying to, and refuses to
write the application when it is not.

3
00:00:11,921 --> 00:00:17,840
I built it because I measured the
workflow it replaced, and that workflow

4
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:20,921
was slower than doing the job by hand.

5
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:27,209
What it saved was not time. It was
two applications out of five that I

6
00:00:27,209 --> 00:00:29,414
should never have started.

7
00:00:29,764 --> 00:00:35,670
Three pieces. The agent loop is one
file. The tools live in a separate

8
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:40,479
process, an M C P server, zero
dependencies. And a model.

9
00:00:40,829 --> 00:00:48,584
The tools are: fetch a posting, check
a G P A gate, log the run. That is all

10
00:00:48,584 --> 00:00:49,400
of them.

11
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:57,036
The design decision I want to point out
is that this is a loop, not a chain.

12
00:00:57,386 --> 00:01:03,103
In the version before this I carried
text between five fixed prompts by

13
00:01:03,103 --> 00:01:08,900
hand. I decided what happened next.
Here the model decides which tool to

14
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,671
call and when to stop.

15
00:01:11,021 --> 00:01:17,074
So the number of steps is not knowable
before it runs, and that is the

16
00:01:17,074 --> 00:01:20,879
actual line between a
workflow and an agent.

17
00:01:21,229 --> 00:01:27,013
One thing first. This dashboard imports
the same function the command line

18
00:01:27,013 --> 00:01:32,954
calls, so every line you see appear is
the agent emitting an event live, not

19
00:01:32,954 --> 00:01:33,657
a replay.

20
00:01:34,007 --> 00:01:40,051
S P A R is a real research fellowship
with applications open. Watch which

21
00:01:40,051 --> 00:01:41,293
tools it calls.

22
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:49,141
It fetched the posting. Now it has a
check G P A gate tool available, and it

23
00:01:49,141 --> 00:01:55,357
is not calling it, because S P
A R states no G P A requirement.

24
00:01:55,707 --> 00:02:02,393
A tool that runs with no reason to
run is a defect, not a bonus. That

25
00:02:02,393 --> 00:02:06,850
restraint is one of the
six things I test for.

26
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:13,714
Verdict: apply. And the history table
on the right picks it up, because that

27
00:02:13,714 --> 00:02:16,629
is a file on disk, not a variable.

28
00:02:16,979 --> 00:02:24,124
Same agent, different posting. K A U
S T states a minimum G P A of three

29
00:02:24,124 --> 00:02:26,407
point five out of four.

30
00:02:26,757 --> 00:02:33,561
There. It called the G P A gate on its
own. I never told it to. It read the

31
00:02:33,561 --> 00:02:39,186
threshold off the posting and
decided the check was necessary.

32
00:02:39,536 --> 00:02:46,864
Now look at what came back. Pass or
fail, and the threshold tested. Not my G

33
00:02:46,864 --> 00:02:47,250
P A.

34
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:52,683
The number lives in a git-ignored
file the model never sees. The tool

35
00:02:52,683 --> 00:02:57,029
answers the question without
the answer leaving my machine.

36
00:02:57,379 --> 00:03:03,135
Verdict: skip. And notice there is
no email. When the answer is skip it

37
00:03:03,135 --> 00:03:08,892
produces nothing to send, because a
polished email for an application I

38
00:03:08,892 --> 00:03:12,379
cannot make is worse
than no output at all.

39
00:03:12,729 --> 00:03:18,412
Here are the real numbers. Six eval
cases written before the agent existed.

40
00:03:18,412 --> 00:03:24,172
Nine out of nine on the mechanical
assertions, but only nine out of fourteen

41
00:03:24,172 --> 00:03:25,157
on judgement.

42
00:03:25,507 --> 00:03:32,508
E four and E five are the weak ones.
It does not reliably say no evidence

43
00:03:32,508 --> 00:03:39,221
for a skill I do not have. That is
a prompt problem I have not solved.

44
00:03:39,571 --> 00:03:46,918
And the limitation I most want to show
you is this. When I ran these evals,

45
00:03:46,918 --> 00:03:49,857
E two, the G P A case, failed.

46
00:03:50,207 --> 00:03:56,685
Not because the model was wrong.
Because I had cut the posting fetch from

47
00:03:56,685 --> 00:04:02,986
six thousand characters to two and
a half thousand to stay under a rate

48
00:04:02,986 --> 00:04:07,779
limit, and K A U S T states
its minimum past that cut.

49
00:04:08,129 --> 00:04:14,110
So the agent never saw the requirement,
reasoned correctly that there was

50
00:04:14,110 --> 00:04:19,271
not one, and told me to apply to
a programme I cannot get into.

51
00:04:19,621 --> 00:04:25,019
A performance optimisation had silently
become a correctness failure, in the

52
00:04:25,019 --> 00:04:30,203
exact behaviour that justifies the
agent existing. An eval I wrote before

53
00:04:30,203 --> 00:04:32,050
any of the code caught it.

54
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:37,522
One last thing. This agent cannot
send anything. No email tool, no form

55
00:04:37,522 --> 00:04:39,686
filling. Not disabled, absent.

56
00:04:40,036 --> 00:04:45,427
Sending is the only irreversible action
here, so the guardrail is that the

57
00:04:45,427 --> 00:04:47,321
capability does not exist.
